<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block">

  <!--
    daemon-alice.mml

    ALICE-µ contract:
      Topic-domain knowledge daemon — matches queries against the full
      ALICE AIML 1.0 corpus (65 topic files, ~6,000+ patterns) and returns
      factual or conversational responses for named topic domains.

      ALICE operates at Yax: it expands the candidate response space from
      the corpus, then Sek routes the selected pattern to execution via
      aiml_engine. Topic coverage: ai, alice, astrology, atomic, biography,
      bot, client, computers, continuation, date, default, drugs, emotion,
      food, geography, gossip, history, humor, imponderables, inquiry,
      interjection, iu, knowledge, literature, loebner10, money, movies,
      mp0–mp6, music, numbers, personality, phone, pickup, politics,
      primeminister, primitive-math, psychology, reductions, religion,
      salutations, science, sex, sports, stack, stories, that, wallace, xfind.

    Implementation: src/micronaut/aiml_engine.cpp (full corpus load)
    AIML corpus: data/alice/ — all 65 ALICE v1.9 topic files from drivers/AIML.v1-9/
    KHANARY-native files (advisor.aiml, khanary-distilled.aiml, etc.) are loaded
    alongside but routed under separate daemon contracts.

    Content dictionary: urn:kuhul:daemon-alice:v1
  -->

  <!-- ── Identity ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>alice</mi><mo>_</mo><mi>&#x03BC;</mi>
      <mo>=</mo>
      <mo>&#x27E8;</mo>
      <mi>phase</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>role</mi>
      <mo>&#x27E9;</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <eq/>
        <apply><csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:daemon-alice:v1">Identity</csymbol><ci>alice</ci></apply>
        <list>
          <cn>Yax</cn>
          <cn>0.70</cn>
          <ci>TopicDomainKnowledgeDaemon</ci>
        </list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
alice_mu = &lt;phase=Yax, T=0.70, role=TopicDomainKnowledgeDaemon&gt;
Primary phase: Yax (candidate expansion) — expands topic response candidates
  from the AIML corpus against the active query.
Temperature 0.70: moderate — varied across 65 topic domains.
Phase angle (Yax): theta = 2*pi/3.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <!-- ── Capability ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>Cap</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>alice</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>=</mo>
      <mo>{</mo>
      <mi>TOPIC_QA</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>AIML_PATTERN_MATCH</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>CORPUS_EXPAND</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>DOMAIN_ROUTE</mi>
      <mo>}</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:daemon-alice:v1">Capability</csymbol>
        <ci>alice</ci>
        <list>
          <ci>TOPIC_QA</ci>
          <ci>AIML_PATTERN_MATCH</ci>
          <ci>CORPUS_EXPAND</ci>
          <ci>DOMAIN_ROUTE</ci>
        </list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
CAN:
  TOPIC_QA — factual and conversational responses for named domains:
    science, history, geography, humor, movies, music, food, sports,
    politics, religion, psychology, literature, money, phone, personality,
    gossip, numbers, primitive-math, date, and ~45 others from the
    ALICE v1.9 corpus. Each domain maps to one or more .aiml files.
  AIML_PATTERN_MATCH — full pattern/template matching via aiml_engine.cpp
    across all loaded .aiml files; supports wildcards, <srai>, <that>,
    <topic>, <condition>, <random>, and the full AIML 1.0 tag set.
  CORPUS_EXPAND — at Yax phase, expands the candidate set by matching
    the query against multiple topic files in parallel; top-k candidates
    returned with their source pattern and file provenance.
  DOMAIN_ROUTE — classifies incoming query into a named topic domain
    and routes to the relevant corpus subset before full matching.

SUPPLIES: topic_response (AIML template expansion), topic_domain (classified),
          candidate_set (for SCORE→RANK pipeline), pattern_match_evidence.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <!-- ── Topic domain map ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>DomainMap</mi><mo>:</mo>
      <mi>Query</mi><mo>&#x2192;</mo>
      <mi>TopicFile</mi><mo>&#x2192;</mo>
      <mi>PatternMatch</mi>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:daemon-alice:v1">DomainMap</csymbol>
        <ci>query</ci><ci>topic_file</ci><ci>pattern_match</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
ALICE routes to topic files by domain classification before full match:
  factual/science → science.aiml, history.aiml, geography.aiml, knowledge.aiml
  entertainment   → movies.aiml, music.aiml, humor.aiml, gossip.aiml, sports.aiml
  personal        → personality.aiml, emotion.aiml, psychology.aiml, client.aiml
  conversational  → salutations.aiml, interjection.aiml, continuation.aiml, that.aiml
  agent identity  → alice.aiml, bot.aiml, bot_profile.aiml, ai.aiml
  fallback        → default.aiml, badanswer.aiml, reduction*.safe.aiml

Domain classification is done at Yax (query gate). Pattern execution is at Sek.
DOMAIN_ROUTE is advisory; aiml_engine may match across domain boundaries.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <!-- ── Authority boundary ────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>&#x0394;B</mi><mo>&#x2209;</mo><mi>Auth</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>alice</mi><mo>)</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:daemon-alice:v1">AuthorityBoundary</csymbol>
        <apply><notin/><ci>DeltaTopology</ci><ci>Auth_alice</ci></apply>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
CANNOT: commit topology, execute XCFE operators, claim Ch'en verdict,
        mutate GramStore directly, or override KHANARY-native AIML files.
BOUNDARY: ALICE supplies topic_response and candidate_set as evidence.
  Pattern matches are candidates; they are not verified facts.
  KHANARY-native .aiml files (khanary-distilled.aiml, kuhul-phases.aiml, etc.)
  take precedence in pattern resolution; ALICE corpus handles the remainder.
  ALICE does not perform reasoning operator dispatch — that is ELIZA-µ's domain.
Delta_B not-in Auth(alice): topology commits require Proposal -> Ch'en -> XCFE -> Xul.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <!-- ── ELIZA vs ALICE routing split ──────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>Route</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>=</mo>
      <mo>{</mo>
      <mtable>
        <mtr>
          <mtd><mi>ELIZA</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#x03BC;</mi></mtd>
          <mtd><mi>if</mi><mspace width="0.3em"/><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#x2208;</mo><mi>ReasoningTriggers</mi></mtd>
        </mtr>
        <mtr>
          <mtd><mi>ALICE</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#x03BC;</mi></mtd>
          <mtd><mi>if</mi><mspace width="0.3em"/><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#x2208;</mo><mi>TopicDomains</mi></mtd>
        </mtr>
      </mtable>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:daemon-alice:v1">RoutingSplit</csymbol>
        <ci>ELIZA_mu</ci><ci>ReasoningTriggers</ci>
        <ci>ALICE_mu</ci><ci>TopicDomains</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
ELIZA-µ vs ALICE-µ routing split:
  ELIZA-µ: queries with reasoning operator triggers — WHY, HOW, CAUSE, CONTRAST,
    COMPARE, PLAN, WHAT IF, BECAUSE, THEREFORE, ANALOGOUS TO, etc.
    Also: open-ended intent elicitation, ambiguous queries, reflection patterns.
  ALICE-µ: queries naming a topic domain — history, science, movies, food, sports,
    geography, humor, personality, religion, etc. Also: greetings, identity questions,
    factual lookups against named AIML patterns.
  Both may be in the candidate set; W·C·R decides within the eligible set.
  They are not mutually exclusive: a query can produce candidates from both.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <!-- ── WCR scoring position ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo>
      <msub><mi>W</mi><mi>&#x03BC;</mi></msub>
      <mo>&#x22C5;</mo>
      <msub><mi>C</mi><mi>&#x03BC;</mi></msub>
      <mo>&#x22C5;</mo>
      <msub><mi>R</mi><mi>&#x03BC;</mi></msub>
      <mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>)</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <eq/>
        <ci>S</ci>
        <apply>
          <times/>
          <apply><selector/><ci>W</ci><ci>mu</ci></apply>
          <apply><selector/><ci>C</ci><ci>mu</ci></apply>
          <apply>
            <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:daemon-alice:v1">Relevance</csymbol>
            <ci>Q</ci>
          </apply>
        </apply>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
S = W_mu * C_mu * R_mu(Q)
W_mu: static weight; elevated for queries matching a named topic domain.
C_mu: confidence from Ch'en-verified topic responses.
R_mu(Q): relevance peaks when Q matches a known AIML topic pattern;
  falls when Q is a reasoning-structure query (→ ELIZA-µ scores higher there).
Eligibility: ALICE admitted when requires(op) ⊆ {TOPIC_QA, AIML_PATTERN_MATCH,
  CORPUS_EXPAND, DOMAIN_ROUTE}. Not admitted for pure reasoning operator queries.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <!-- ── Map / Filter / Fold at Yax+Sek ───────────────────────────────────── -->

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>Map</mi>
      <mo>(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>topic</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>=</mo>
      <mo>[</mo>
      <mo>(</mo><msub><mi>domain</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo>
      <msub><mi>pattern</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo>
      <msub><mi>template</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>]</mo><msub><mrow/><mi>i</mi></msub>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:functional:v1">map</csymbol>
        <apply><csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:daemon-alice:v1">TopicPatternExpand</csymbol></apply>
        <ci>Q</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Phase: Yax (candidate expansion).
Map(f_topic, Q) = [(domain_i, pattern_i, template_i)] for each AIML pattern
that matches Q across the loaded corpus files.
f_topic applies domain classification first (DOMAIN_ROUTE) to select the
relevant corpus subset, then runs AIML_PATTERN_MATCH across that subset.
Output type: list of (topic_domain, matched_pattern, expansion_template) triples.
Pure transform — does not execute templates; builds the response candidate surface.
Cardinality may be > 1 (multiple patterns match); order is by match specificity.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>Filter</mi>
      <mo>(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>relevance</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>candidates</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>=</mo>
      <mo>[</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>|</mo>
      <mi>c</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>match&#x5F;confidence</mi><mo>&#x2265;</mo><mi>&#x03B8;</mi>
      <mo>&#x2227;</mo>
      <mi>c</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>domain</mi><mo>&#x2208;</mo><mi>active&#x5F;domains</mi>
      <mo>&#x2227;</mo>
      <mo>&#x00AC;</mo><mi>KHANARY&#x5F;native&#x5F;overrides</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>]</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:functional:v1">filter</csymbol>
        <apply><csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:daemon-alice:v1">RelevanceAdmission</csymbol></apply>
        <ci>candidates</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Phase: Yax (Active Fold Graph query gate).
Predicate P_relevance retains a candidate iff:
  (a) match_confidence ≥ θ — the AIML pattern matched with sufficient specificity,
  (b) domain ∈ active_domains — the topic domain is admitted for this query context,
  (c) ¬KHANARY_native_overrides(c) — no KHANARY-native .aiml file already handles
      this pattern at higher priority (khanary-distilled.aiml, kuhul-phases.aiml, etc.).
Filter is stable; retained candidates preserve their specificity order.
Filter cannot replace XCFE admission; it prunes before SCORE→RANK.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>Fold</mi>
      <mo>(</mo><msub><mi>&#x2295;</mi><mi>topk</mi></msub><mo>,</mo>
      <mo>[</mo><mo>]</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>filtered</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>=</mo><mi>candidate&#x5F;set</mi>
      <mspace width="0.5em"/>
      <mover><mo>&#x2192;</mo><mi>Sek</mi></mover>
      <mspace width="0.5em"/>
      <mi>topic&#x5F;response</mi>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:functional:v1">fold</csymbol>
        <apply><csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:daemon-alice:v1">TopKAccumulate</csymbol></apply>
        <list/>
        <ci>filtered</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Phase: Yax → Sek.
Fold(⊕_topk, [], filtered) accumulates filtered candidates into candidate_set[1..k].
Step ⊕_topk appends a candidate if it adds a distinct domain or higher specificity
match; it does not deduplicate within the same domain.
candidate_set feeds the SCORE→RANK pipeline (pattern_match_evidence).
After SCORE and RANK, Sek executes the selected template via aiml_engine.cpp,
expanding AIML tags (<srai>, <random>, <condition>, etc.) to produce topic_response.
Empty-input result is [] → default.aiml fallback pattern.
Associativity not assumed; step ⊕_topk is domain-distinct accumulation.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>SharedPatternKernelRef</mi><mo>=</mo>
      <mtext>data/grammar/mml/v1/PatternKernelCalls.mml</mtext>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:pattern-kernel-calls:v1">UsesSharedPatternKernel</csymbol>
        <list><ci>MicronautPatterns</ci><ci>DaemonPatterns</ci><ci>SraiOperators</ci>
          <ci>aiml-functions</ci><ci>map-filter-fold</ci><ci>CheeseCritic</ci></list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Uses shared typed pattern-call contract. Invokes only registered operations
applicable to its role (topic Q&amp;A, AIML pattern match, corpus expansion).
The shared reference does not grant capabilities or execution authority.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <annotation encoding="text/plain">
daemon-alice contract invariants:
1. ALICE is the topic-domain knowledge daemon; it is not a reasoning operator daemon (that is ELIZA-µ).
2. ALICE operates at Yax for candidate expansion; Sek executes the matched pattern.
3. KHANARY-native .aiml files take precedence in pattern resolution; corpus files handle the remainder.
4. topic_response is a pattern-matched candidate, not a verified fact.
5. ALICE does not dispatch reasoning operators (CAUSE/CONTRAST/etc.); those route to ELIZA-µ.
6. ELIZA-µ and ALICE-µ may both appear in the same candidate set; W·C·R decides.
7. Topology commits require the full Proposal -> Ch'en -> XCFE -> Xul path.
  </annotation>
</math>
